[SIZE=6][B][COLOR=#00b8d4]ARMOR SWAP[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE]
[SIZE=4][I]Bring Modern Minecraft's Right-Click Armor Swapping — and More — to Every Version[/I][/SIZE]
[SIZE=3][COLOR=#888888]Supports Minecraft [B]1.8 – 1.21+[/B]  •  Spigot  •  Paper  •  Purpur  •  [B]Folia[/B][/COLOR][/SIZE]
[COLOR=#cccccc]────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────[/COLOR][/CENTER]

[SIZE=5][B][COLOR=#00b8d4]✦ Why ArmorSwap?[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE]
Minecraft 1.19.4 introduced right-click armor hot-swapping in vanilla—leaving older servers behind, and stopping short of what players actually want.

[B]ArmorSwap[/B] brings seamless right-click armor and Elytra swapping back to [B]every server version from 1.8 to 1.21+[/B], and goes far beyond vanilla by letting players swap entire armor sets with [B]Armor Stands[/B], swap worn or held gear with [B]Item Frames[/B], equip custom hats with [B]/armorswap head[/B], and toggle swapping per player!

[CENTER][COLOR=#cccccc]────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────[/COLOR][/CENTER]

[SIZE=5][B][COLOR=#00b8d4]✦ Key Features[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*][B]Right-Click Main-Hand Armor & Elytra Swap[/B]
Right-click while holding any helmet, chestplate, Elytra, leggings, or boots to instantly swap it with the piece you are currently wearing.
[I]Smart Block Detection:[/I] Right-clicking chests, doors, anvils, furnaces, and other interactable blocks opens them normally unless you are sneaking!

[*][B]Full Armor Stand Swapping (Shift + Right-Click)[/B]
Sneak and right-click any Armor Stand to swap your entire worn armor set with the stand in a single click! If the Armor Stand has arms, your main-hand items swap too. Automatically respects invisible stands and 1.16+ equipment locks.

[*][B]Item Frame Swapping (Shift + Right-Click)[/B]
Sneak and right-click an Item Frame to swap your held item with the displayed item—or shift-right-click an armor piece on a frame with an [B]empty hand[/B] to swap it directly with the armor you're wearing! Respects fixed/locked item frames.

[*][B]Hat / Head Command (/armorswap head)[/B]
Place any held block or item directly onto your helmet slot (and swap your old helmet back into your hand or inventory). Properly handles stacked items by placing a single item on your head.

[*][B]Per-Player Toggle (/armorswap)[/B]
Players can enable or disable armor swapping for themselves at any time. Preferences are saved automatically via PersistentDataContainer (1.14+) or [FONT=Courier New]playerdata.yml[/FONT] (1.8–1.13).

[*][B]Curse of Binding & Protection Plugin Support[/B]
Strictly respects [B]Curse of Binding[/B] across all swaps and commands (with an optional config toggle or [FONT=Courier New]armorswap.bypass.enchantment[/FONT] permission). Works seamlessly with [B]WorldGuard[/B], [B]GriefPrevention[/B], [B]Kingdoms[/B], and other region/claim protection plugins.

[*][B]Multi-Version & Folia Native[/B]
One lightweight JAR runs cleanly from [B]1.8.8 through 1.21.x[/B] with native [B]Folia[/B] regional scheduler support and cached configuration lookups for zero lag.
[/LIST]

